# K.1: alternating central quotients

The faithful-action cover reduction gives actual alternating or triple-cover
isomorphisms. Both ratios of the six-dimensional natural A₇ action are 3/2;
their source application retains the actual module intertwiner. Quasiequivalence
transport preserves the cubic and quadratic indexing families separately.

The remaining representation recognition and FF-offender calculations are
independent obligations before `Alternating.Conclusion` can be obtained from
`Alternating.Input`. The shared contracts do not assert those classifications.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), K.1, pp.452–453.
-/
